<title>USA: Unocal does not expect refinery strike.</title>
<headline>Unocal does not expect refinery strike.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Unocal Corp spokesman said on Monday he did not believe there would be a strike at four California refineries the company is selling to Tosco Corp.</p>
<p>Tosco announced earlier it had reached a tentative agreement with the Oil, Chemical and Atomic Workers Union (OCAW) on a new labour contract for the refineries after it assumes ownership on March 31.</p>
<p>The OCAW, which represents 900 workers at the four refineries, still has outstanding issues with Unocal relating to the sale of the refineries and says a strike remains an option if Unocal refuses to negotiate.</p>
<p>&quot;We still don't believe there's going to be a strike,&quot; Unocal spokesman Barry Lane said, adding that the company was still &quot;having conversations&quot; with the union.</p>
</text>
